(:id "port/luau/packet" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireReadsTheGoldens" "internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireReadNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luau/write_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireWritesTheGoldens" "internal/codegen/luau/write_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireWriteNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauSelectedArmStartsAtItsDefaults" "internal/codegen/luau/serialize_vendor_test.go: TestVendoredLuauSerializeIsThePin" "make packet-utf8-luau, packet-utf8-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-wide-luau, packet-wide-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-defaults-luau, packet-defaults-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-finite-luau, packet-finite-luau-negative-control (make/luau.mk)" "make schema-luau-generated-analyze-strict-gate, schema-luau-generated-analyze-strict-gate-negative-control") :tested-revision "2f56f1130ea5c4bf3a4152fec1ca66349081be6d" :note "2026-11-04: The Luau packet leg (internal/codegen/luau, the vendored serialize.luau) reads and writes every shared packet golden byte-identical to C++, with a read and a write negative control that go red. The four packet gates pass on the pin with their controls: packet-text (33 pinned rows and 496 bit flips agree with C++, 192 mutated refusals), packet-wide (32 pinned rows and 1016 bit flips agree with C++, 503 mutated refusals), packet-defaults and packet-finite. The generated code passes luau-analyze --mode=strict, and its planted-pattern control goes red. Run on hetzner1 (Linux x86-64) at main 2f56f1130 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/build-version" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/buildversion_test.go: TestLuauBuildVersion, TestLuauBuildVersionNegativeControl, TestLuauBuildVersionNegativeControl/constant, TestLuauBuildVersionNegativeControl/block-check, TestLuauBuildVersionNegativeControl/cook-write, TestLuauBuildVersionNegativeControl/cook-check") :tested-revision "ba0c55b06217fa9fe54020914e61db5915cdddc3" :note "2026-11-04: tables/block's generated PaddedFrameBlock.buildVersion and TableMessageBuildVersion equal ir.BuildVersion and the version the C++ reference stamped into block_padded.bin and block_render.bin; each of the 64 version bits of the C++ block and of a written cook refuses wrong_build_version, ahead of truncation and the alignment word; the cook writer stamps the version at byte 8 in both byte orders. The constant, block-check, cook-write and cook-check controls each turn exactly their own clauses red. Run on hetzner2 (Linux x86-64) at ba0c55b06 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/block-read" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/block_read_test.go: TestLuauBlockReadAgreesWithGo" "internal/codegen/luautable/block_read_control_test.go: TestLuauBlockOpenClauses, TestLuauBlockOpenClausesNegativeControl, TestLuauBlockOpenClausesNegativeControl/stride, TestLuauBlockOpenClausesNegativeControl/count, TestLuauBlockOpenClausesNegativeControl/version" "./build/conformance-harness run --only luau: block 2/2, block-foreign 2/2, block-dump 2/2, forgery 13/13, block-reason 13/13") :tested-revision "ba0c55b06217fa9fe54020914e61db5915cdddc3" :note "2026-11-04: The reflective read lands the records the generated Go builder wrote and every damaged block refuses by the name Go's BlockOpen answers; the C++ reference image opens through the generated PaddedFrameBlock and each forged clause answers Go's verdict; cutting the stride, count or version clause turns exactly that case red. The harness's block surfaces all pass. Run on hetzner2 (Linux x86-64) at ba0c55b06 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/cook-write" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/cook_write_test.go: TestLuauCookMatchesTheGoCook" "internal/codegen/luautable/cook_corpus_test.go: TestLuauCookWritesCommittedCorpus" "internal/codegen/luautable/cook_inline_bytes_test.go: TestLuauCookWritesInlineByteArrays, TestLuauCookWritesInlineByteArraysNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luautable/cook_order_control_test.go: TestLuauCookOrderWordNegativeControl" "./build/conformance-harness run --only luau: cook-write 142/142") :tested-revision "ba0c55b06217fa9fe54020914e61db5915cdddc3" :note "2026-11-04: The cook writer matches internal/tablecook byte for byte, with CookMeasure the length and the data-cycle and invalid-union refusals Go's; every committed cook-write row executes; the record a constructor builds and a record with populated [N]uint8 and [E]uint8 cook to the tool's bytes (the writer read those buffers as lists and threw before this change; its control restores that and goes red). Run on hetzner2 (Linux x86-64) at ba0c55b06 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
(:id "port/luau/vt/unit-registry" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luautable/unit_view_corpus_test.go: TestLuauUnitViewCorpus" "internal/codegen/luautable/unit_view_corpus_test.go: TestLuauUnitViewNegativeControl, TestLuauUnitViewNegativeControl/unflattened, TestLuauUnitViewNegativeControl/drop, TestLuauUnitViewNegativeControl/doc, TestLuauUnitViewNegativeControl/id" "internal/codegen/luautable/unit_registry_test.go: TestLuauUnitViewListsTheUnit, TestLuauUnitViewTableFree" "internal/codegen/luautable/type_view_test.go: TestLuauEveryTypeHasAView") :tested-revision "ba0c55b06217fa9fe54020914e61db5915cdddc3" :note "2026-11-04: schema_view.luau's UnitView() lists 50 of 50 units (the VIEW_CORPUS units and the tables manifest) byte-equal to internal/viewlisting; the registry and its rows are frozen; a table-free unit gets the view alone; every type has a descriptor, a type no table reaches with no wire identity. The unflattened, drop, doc and id controls each go red on the line they own. Run on hetzner2 (Linux x86-64) at ba0c55b06 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1 SCHEMA_REQUIRE_CORPUS=1.")
